ON PACKAGES` ACE, despite having an AppContainer package SID. This pattern suggests a possible Chromium/Electron sandbox interaction issue. The sandbox requires `ALL APPLICATION PACKAGES` if any AppContainer ACE exists.\n\n\nApplying a specific security identifier grants access to sandboxed processes, enabling program execution. This configuration successfully addresses the runtime issue in both the Gemini and Antigravity applications. Now reviewing the plan-driven execution rule for the Antigravity 2.0 implementation.\n\n\nTo ensure proper execution, before proceeding with any modifications, two artifact files, a task list and implementation plan, must be created within the designated directory and submitted for review. This is essential for clarity and approval.\n\nAlso, re-confirming that the user recently installed Gemini, which is crashing after install due to a sandbox security check; the root cause is missing access control list entries in the application's directory, triggering a permission error.\n\n\nThe Gemini application crashes due to the absence of the required security identifier within its directory, blocking the process. The Antigravity application, though running, fails to display a window; this is due to disabled rendering and likely missing security identifiers as well. Applying the security identifier and cleaning up the shortcut arguments should address both application issues. Reviewing the artifact directory path for Gemini-related files.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"안티그래비티 및 제미나이 네이티브 앱 실행 불가 오류 해결을 위한 작업 단계 목록","UserFacing":true},"CodeContent":"# 작업 목록 (Task List): 네이티브 앱 실행 불가 원인 분석 및 해결\n\n- [/] **1. 긴급 원인 분석 (Research)** <!-- id: 0 -->\n    - [x] 실행 프로세스 및 백그라운드 상태 점검 <!-- id: 1 -->\n    - [x] 최근 다운로드 및 설치 경로 조사 (`GeminiSetup.exe`, `Antigravity 2.23.1`) <!-- id: 2 -->\n    - [x] 윈도우 이벤트 로그 및 크래시 덤프(`CrashDumps/*.dmp`) 추적 <!-- id: 3 -->\n    - [x] Electron 샌드박스